          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 210,
          "message": "The Linux worker has no hard total-memory cap. Use a cgroup limit where available; periodic working-set sampling can terminate the worker only after it has already exceeded 512 MB.",
          "confidence": 0.82,
          "category": "security A06:2025",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "On Linux, the worker is launched with a prlimit --data limit, while Supervise checks its working set every 25 ms and kills it only after a sample exceeds the limit. This does not impose a total memory cap on the process.",
            "failureScenario": "A crafted PDF causes memory growth outside the data limit or a rapid working-set spike. The worker can exceed 512 MB before the next sample triggers termination, so the configured limit does not prevent that memory use."
